# L040: a data file (the host dialect: `host` / `list` / `mesh` / `tree` / `fuse` and literals) that breaks a rule of
# its grammar: a key given twice, a value beside children, an anchor declared after data, a fuse of an unknown anchor,
# a bare word where text belongs. The rules and their messages live in the data reader (compile/host-data.tree,
# note/term/host/01-grammar.md); this reports them so `term lint` and the editor show a data file's problems the way
# they show a program's: the reader's diagnostics when it refuses the file, else the expander's.
#
# Ported from lint/rules/data-grammar.ts (self-hosting, 2026-10-06), which stays as the face: it is the rule object the
# lint driver holds, and it writes each report as a finding under the rule's name, code and severity.

load @term/base/list
  find list

load ../parser/tree
  find root-node

load ../compile/host-data
  find read-data
  find expand-data

load ./rule-check
  find rule-report

task data-reports
  take tree, like root-node
  take file, like text
  like list, like rule-report

  save out, make list
  save diagnostics, make list
  save read, read-data(tree, file, false)
  fork test, read/ok
    hold
      save expanded, expand-data(read/file, file)
      save diagnostics, expanded/diagnostics
    miss
      save diagnostics, read/diagnostics
  walk diagnostics
    take one
    save report
      make rule-report
        bind message, one/message
        bind span, one/span
    push(out, report)
  back out
